# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/.next-preview/
/.next-verify/
/out/

# production
/build

# data books — ingestion sources only. Manufacturer PDFs are never committed
# or redistributed (see data/packs/AGENTS.md and the data-usage rules in
# docs/universal-table-schema.md); only the facts extracted from them are.
/data/books/*
!/data/books/README.md

# voice bake-off — the harness is committed, the evidence never is. Recordings
# are real voices on real sites; the case files and the vocabulary carry client
# names and street addresses (see bakeoff/README.md).
/bakeoff/audio/*
!/bakeoff/audio/README.md
/bakeoff/cases/*
!/bakeoff/cases/README.md
/bakeoff/results/
/bakeoff/vocab.json

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.claude/settings.local.json

# build output when -o .next-build is used for verification builds
.next-build/

# iCloud's duplicate files. ~/Desktop is an iCloud folder, so when the daemon
# resolves a sync conflict it writes a SECOND copy beside the original —
# `day-rail.test 2.ts` next to `day-rail.test.ts` — with the same contents it
# had at the moment of the conflict. They are invisible in an editor's file
# tree and easy to sweep up with `git add -A`; 239 of them reached main that
# way (#576), including 108 test files, and jest ran every one.
#
# A stale copy of a test is worse than dead weight: it goes on asserting the
# behaviour the real file has since moved away from, so the NEXT change to the
# real file fails CI in a file nobody edited. That is exactly how it surfaced.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*
* copy.*
* copy [0-9].*
